                            <comment id="500997" author="adilger" created="Sat, 5 Sep 2026 04:53:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=colmstea&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;colmstea&quot;&gt;colmstea&lt;/a&gt;, any chance to look into this?  Trying to test patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/66617&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66617&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20356&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_398c: FAIL: 52% of I/O are 1-page on large PAGE_SIZE clients &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20356&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20356&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: sanity/398c margin for large PAGE_SIZE&quot;) with &quot;&lt;tt&gt;Test-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=398c,ONLY_REPEAT=100 clientarch=aarch64&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; but it failed with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Untestable Enforced:
    Test-Parameters line #1: custom on el9.7-x86_64/el9.7-aarch64/ldiskfs/ldiskfs
        client: el9.7 - aarch64 | lustre-reviews #131059

Supported build configurations for lustre-reviews #131059:
Clients
    rocky9.5 - aarch64 - inkernel
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It would be better to have it auto-select the distro to match an available build based on the specified &lt;tt&gt;clientarch&lt;/tt&gt; if it is not specified..&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
